Recommended immediate plan: structured debug metadata + PE CodeView (RSDS) parsing

Add the following actionable plan (checklist) to increase parity by focusing on structured debug metadata and implementing PDB extraction for PE. This plan is intentionally incremental, test-first, and low-risk.

A) Design common debug metadata API (src/common.zig)
- [ ] Add debug_type enum { none, pdb, dwarf, dsym, other }
- [ ] Add debug_metadata optional struct union with variants for pdb/dwarf/dsym including fields:
    - pdb: { path: []const u8, guid: ?[16]u8, age: ?u32 }
    - dwarf/dsym: { uuid: ?[16]u8, path: []const u8 }
- [ ] Keep debug_info_present for quick checks (derive from debug_type != none)

B) Update ownership & free logic
- [ ] Update root.freeBinaryDescription (and BinaryBundle.free if used) to free any allocator-owned memory in debug_metadata
- [ ] Update freeImportEntries / free helpers if they need to free new debug slices
- [ ] Add unit test that exercises freeBinaryDescription with debug metadata populated to catch leaks

C) Implement CodeView/RSDS parsing in decodePESlice
- [ ] Parse IMAGE_DEBUG_DIRECTORY entries (use existing debug_rva/debug_sz discovery)
- [ ] Locate CodeView entries and detect RSDS signature
- [ ] Extract GUID (16 bytes), age (4 bytes), and the NUL-terminated PDB path string
- [ ] Allocate owned copy of PDB path and populate BinaryDescription.debug_metadata.pdb fields; set debug_type = .pdb and debug_info_present = true
- [ ] Append a short message if parsing fails but a debug directory exists

D) Tests & fixture
- [ ] Add testing/assets/pe-pdb-codeview.exe (or minimal synthetic fixture containing a valid IMAGE_DEBUG_DIRECTORY + RSDS block)
- [ ] Add unit test asserting:
    - desc.debug_info_present == true
    - desc.debug_type == .pdb
    - debug_metadata.pdb.path equals expected string
    - debug_metadata.pdb.guid and age parsed (when present)
- [ ] Ensure test calls root.freeBinaryDescription to avoid leaks

E) JSON/pretty-print & docs
- [ ] Update src/json_output.zig and BinaryDescription.writePretty to emit debug_type and debug_metadata in a stable, backward-compatible way (keep debug_pdb_path for one release if desired)
- [ ] Update README.md/docs with a short example showing how to read debug metadata from the JSON output

F) Chronicle & CI
- [ ] Create a chronicle entry describing the change, tests, and commands run
- [ ] Add this test to the regular unit test suite and ensure zig build test passes locally
- [ ] Add CI job or ensure existing CI runs decoder tests that depend on testing/assets

G) Follow-ups (after PE PDB is implemented)
- [ ] Implement minimal DWARF detection for ELF (presence of .debug_info or CU header read) and populate debug_metadata.dwarf
- [ ] Implement Mach-O LC_UUID/dSYM pairing and populate debug_metadata.dsym (uuid/path)
- [ ] Consider adding a tiny SDK helper to resolve dSYMs/PDBs using the structured metadata (out of scope for this core parity task)

